doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24024417
abstract: >
  Committed data and analysis for three pre-registered buyer-side
  experiments verifying x402 v2 payments on Base. A fresh $0.01 mainnet
  settlement verified end-to-end via payer-anchored Transfer events on two
  independent RPCs (paid run 1.11 s; discovery median 0.0388 s over 15
  GETs). Four of four hostile-seller failure modes were correctly
  detected, including a same-nonce EIP-3009 replay that reverted at EVM
  state level on an Anvil fork pinned at block 54035433. Two of three
  third-party endpoints returned protocol-compatible v2 402 challenges;
  agent402.tools diverged with a 404. Zero payment-bearing headers were
  sent in the third-party probe.
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - pre-registered-experiment
